  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 314 AM MDT THU OCT 15 2026\ncold front moving across our area Sunday will help drop peak \ntemperatures a few degrees, but will still be 5 to 10 degrees above \nnormal. Monday through Tuesday, our area will come under a strong \nsouthwest flow ahead of an incoming Pacific upper low from the Gulf \nof Alaska. This flow pattern will keep Monday slightly warmer than \nnormal with elevated wind breezes from the south. There is better \nlong-term guidance agreement on the upper low diving south along the \nnorthwest and California coasts before moving inland into the Great \nBasin Tuesday through Thursday. This pattern will return a cooldown \nand chances of precipitation over our area late Tuesday through \nThursday. There remains some uncertainty over the magnitude and \ncoverage extent of this potential multi-day precipitation event next \nweek, especially for Tuesday and Wednesday. For now, next Thursday \nis looking to have the highest potential for areawide precipitation \nas the upper low crosses the Great Basin.",
